    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Club Canin Dracenois, on boulevard Général Leclerc in Draguignan, has a large secure ground where dogs and owners can take training classes, from puppy to adult, up to competition preparation.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>As with any club run by volunteers, it's best to contact the club beforehand to find out opening days and hours, which often follow a volunteer-run schedule rather than fixed commercial hours.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: even if you're only passing through the Var, some dog clubs accept drop-in visitors for a single session — it's worth asking.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Draguignan and its town centre are accessible from boulevard Général Leclerc.</p>
